{"command": "cat > /home/test/t508n/work/patch-0001-lse-early-correct.patch <<'EOF'
From: offline-analysis
Subject: [PATCH] T508N: move LSE early alternative patch to IRQ-off/pre-SMP context

The previous hack called t508n_apply_lse_early() from kernel_init_freeable():
- interrupts are already enabled,
- kthreadd/workqueue context exists,
- __apply_alternatives() walks and patches 12k atomics sites without
  stop_machine or IRQ masking,
- icache_inval_all_pou() is currently a dsb(ish) no-op, so the boot CPU
  may keep executing stale (pre-LSE) I-cache lines.

Move the call to smp_prepare_boot_cpu(), immediately after
setup_boot_cpu_features(). At this point:
- local IRQs are still disabled (early_boot_irqs_disabled == true),
- only the boot CPU is online,
- boot alternatives have just been applied.

Then explicitly flush the boot CPU I-cache by VA, matching stock
__flush_icache_range() behaviour (dc cvau + ic ivau), never ic ialluis.

This should make LSE patching deterministic instead of racing with IRQs.

---
 arch/arm64/kernel/alternative.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c         |  3 +++
 init/main.c                     |  6 ------
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/alternative.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/alternative.c
index xxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/alternative.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/alternative.c
@@ -331,6 +331,9 @@ void __init t508n_apply_lse_early(void)
 {
 	u64 isar0;
 	DECLARE_BITMAP(caps, ARM64_NCAPS);
+	extern char _stext[], _etext[];
+
+	WARN_ON(!irqs_disabled());	/* T508N: must run before SMP/IRQ enable */

 	isar0 = read_sanitised_ftr_reg(SYS_ID_AA64ISAR0_EL1);
 	if (!cpuid_feature_extract_unsigned_field(isar0, ID_AA64ISAR0_EL1_ATOMIC_SHIFT))
@@ -343,6 +346,12 @@ void __init t508n_apply_lse_early(void)
 	set_bit(ARM64_HAS_LSE_ATOMICS, system_cpucaps);
 	bitmap_clear(caps, 0, ARM64_NCAPS);
 	set_bit(ARM64_HAS_LSE_ATOMICS, caps);
 	__apply_alternatives(&kernel_alternatives, false, caps);
+
+	/*
+	 * icache_inval_all_pou() is currently dsb(ish) only, so explicitly
+	 * invalidate the boot CPU's I-cache by VA.  Stock 5.4 uses
+	 * dc cvau + ic ivau + dsb ish + isb and never relies on ialluis here.
+	 */
+	__flush_icache_range((unsigned long)_stext, (unsigned long)_etext);
+	isb();
 }

 #ifdef CONFIG_MODULES
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c
index xxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c
@@ -472,6 +472,9 @@ void __init smp_prepare_boot_cpu(void)
 	cpuinfo_store_boot_cpu();
 	setup_boot_cpu_features();

+	extern void t508n_apply_lse_early(void);
+	t508n_apply_lse_early();
+
 	/* Conditionally switch to GIC PMR for interrupt masking */
 	if (system_uses_irq_prio_masking())
 		init_gic_priority_masking();
diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
index xxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1549,12 +1549,6 @@ static noinline void __init kernel_init_freeable(void)

 	cad_pid = get_pid(task_pid(current));

-	/* T508N: SMP 上线前 patch LSE atomics (见 alternative.c) */
-	{
-		extern void t508n_apply_lse_early(void);
-		t508n_apply_lse_early();
-	}
-
 	smp_prepare_cpus(setup_max_cpus);
 	t508n_stage(3); /* smp_prepare_cpus 完成 */
EOF
echo saved patch"}

